      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1963 the American‑Hawaiian Steamship Company bought 12,000 acres and, with Prudential, drafted a master plan that birthed Westlake Village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
