        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wlv.org/116/City-History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Long before settlers, the Chumash lived here, founding the village Hipuc around 500 BCE and harvesting acorns for centuries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        7,
        15,
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.westlakevillage.com/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Westlake’s Russell Ranch hosted classics like Robin Hood, Tarzan, and Bonanza, making the area a Hollywood filming hotspot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westlake_Village%2C_California",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Westlake Village sits nine miles inland from the Pacific, perched in the Santa Monica Mountains’ foothills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wlv.org/116/City-History",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Westlake Lake sits at the community’s heart, around which the master‑planned streets and homes were arranged.",
